  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "RC, transformer and direct coupling"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "RC coupling uses a coupling capacitor and the collector resistor: it is cheap, compact and has a flat response over the audio range, so it is used in voltage amplifier stages; it cannot pass DC and gives poor impedance matching. Transformer coupling gives impedance matching and high efficiency (no DC loss in a collector resistor), so it suits power output stages; it is bulky, costly and has a poorer frequency response. Direct coupling joins stages without any capacitor or transformer, so it amplifies DC and very low frequencies; its operating point drifts with temperature. It is used in op-amps and DC amplifiers."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "RC: cheap, flat audio response; voltage stages"
    },
    {
     "en": "Transformer: impedance matching; power stages"
    },
    {
     "en": "Direct: amplifies DC; suffers drift"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "RC coupling is cheap with a flat audio response, transformer coupling matches impedance, and direct coupling can amplify DC.",
    "kn": "RC ಜೋಡಣೆ ಅಗ್ಗ ಮತ್ತು ಶ್ರವ್ಯ ಪಟ್ಟಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಸಮತಟ್ಟಾದ ಪ್ರತಿಕ್ರಿಯೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ; ಪರಿವರ್ತಕ ಜೋಡಣೆ ಪ್ರತಿರೋಧ ಹೊಂದಾಣಿಕೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ; ನೇರ ಜೋಡಣೆ DC ಯನ್ನೂ ವರ್ಧಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
